    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u explain how a diesel turbocharger actually works? like the step by step of how the exhaust gas makes the boost happen? i need to understand the mechanics for my exam.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A diesel turbocharger converts the thermal energy of high-pressure exhaust gases into mechanical energy to compress fresh air entering the engine. As hot exhaust gases flow through the turbine housing, they strike the turbine wheel, causing it to spin at high speeds driven by engine operation. This spinning turbine is connected via a shaft to the compressor wheels on the front of the assembly, which sucks in and compresses clean intake air much faster than natural aspiration allows. The result is increased boost pressure, cooling the air, and delivering a denser oxygen supply to the combustion chambers for significantly more power.",
      "source": "target",
